From 5e749b22147c879afb74a58be1c310948649f8a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:57:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] test(wire): set taper_deg in the wire_stamp WireContourOp
 literal

#1163 added the taper_deg field to WireContourOp; wire_stamp.rs still
built its literal without it, so the camcraft-app test binary did not
compile on main. Test-only: taper_deg 0.0 (no taper), as the other
wire test literals set it. Every camcraft-app test binary compiles.

Fixes #1377

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/app/tests/wire_stamp.rs | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/crates/app/tests/wire_stamp.rs b/crates/app/tests/wire_stamp.rs
index b9fe2adc7..6b8bc6421 100644
--- a/crates/app/tests/wire_stamp.rs
+++ b/crates/app/tests/wire_stamp.rs
@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@ fn wire_op(side: WireSide, start: Option<[f64; 2]>) -> WireContourOp {
         side,
         start,
         burnout: None,
+        taper_deg: 0.0,
         clearance: operation::DEFAULT_CLEARANCE,
     }
 }
